  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-resolver-dns 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-resolver-dns 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-45673, CVE-2026-45674, and CVE-2026-47691.\n\nCVE-2026-45673: Netty: DNS Cache Poisoning due to Predictable PRNG and Default Static Source Port\n\nCVE-2026-45674: Netty Vulnerable to DNS Cache Poisoning via Missing Bailiwick Checks in CNAME Records\n\nCVE-2026-47691: Netty has Insufficient Bailiwick Validation for NS Records\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-resolver-dns 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.",
